      "text": "The PRA uses the term “material outsourcing” to capture any outsourcing arrangement that, if weak or failed, would seriously jeopardise a firm’s ability to meet the Threshold Conditions or comply with the Fundamental Rules [2].",
      "supported": true,
      "cited_supports": true
    },
    {
      "text": "For PRA purposes, a “material outsourcing” arrangement encompasses any “critical or important outsourcing” arrangement defined in the retained EU legislation (e.g., the EBA Outsourcing Guidelines) [1].",
      "supported": true,
      "cited_supports": true
    },
    {
      "text": "The PRA’s materiality test therefore incorporates the EU concept of a “critical or important operational function”, applying the same criteria used for critical/important outsourcing under EU rules, with only limited PRA‑specific exceptions [8].",
      "supported": true,
      "cited_supports": false
    }
  ],
